<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/During%20the%20initial%20phases%20%28duration%20based%20on%20individual%20features%29%20supervised%2C%20in-hospital%20exercise%20training%20programme%20may%20be%20recommended%2C%20especially%2C%20to%20verify%20individual%20responses%20and%20tolerability%2C%20clinical%20stability%2C%20and%20promptly%20identify%20signs%20and%20symptoms%20indicating%20to%20modify%20or%20terminate%20the%20programme.%20The%20supervision%20should%20include%20physical%20examination%2C%20monitoring%20of%20HR%2C%20BP%20and%20rhythm%20before%2C%20during%20and%20after%20exercise%20training.%20The%20supervised%20period%20should%20be%20prolonged%20in%20patients%20with%20new%20symptoms%2C%20signs%2C%20BP%20abnormalities%20and%20increased%20supraventricular%20or%20ventricular%20ectopy%20during%20exercise> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://digistrucmed.org/ClinicalProcedure> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/All%20smokers%20should%20be%20professionally%20encouraged%20to%20permanently%20stop%20smoking%20all%20forms%20of%20tobacco.%20Follow-up%2C%20referral%20to%20special%20multidisciplinary%20programmes%20and%2For%20pharmacotherapy%20%28including%20nicotine%20replacement%29%20are%20recommended%2C%20as%20a%20stepwise%20strategy%20for%20smoking%20cessation.%20Structured%20approaches%20are%20to%20be%20used%2C%20for%20example%2C%205As:%20Ask%2C%20Advise%2C%20Assess%2C%20Assist%2C%20Arrange> <http://digistrucmed.org/name> "All smokers should be professionally encouraged to permanently stop smoking all forms of tobacco. Follow-up, referral to special multidisciplinary programmes and/or pharmacotherapy (including nicotine replacement) are recommended, as a stepwise strategy for smoking cessation. Structured approaches are to be used, for example, 5As: Ask, Advise, Assess, Assist, Arrange" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/su_verified_0074e29f31a1f0feb082e0064bee46f60bf6b5ae3f8703d1231341374ed97e52_table_1/e_0094> <http://digistrucmed.org/hasNormalization> <http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/su_verified_0074e29f31a1f0feb082e0064bee46f60bf6b5ae3f8703d1231341374ed97e52_table_1/e_0094/normalization> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/Frequency:%20most%20days%20%28at%20least%203%20days%2Fweek%20and%20preferably%206%E2%80%937%20days%2Fweek%29%20for%20aerobic%20training%3B%202%20times%2Fweek%20for%20resistance%2Fstrength%20training> <http://digistrucmed.org/name> "Frequency: most days (at least 3 days/week and preferably 6–7 days/week) for aerobic training; 2 times/week for resistance/strength training" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/su_verified_0074e29f31a1f0feb082e0064bee46f60bf6b5ae3f8703d1231341374ed97e52_table_1/tu_0063> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "No goal for triglycerides, but  $< 1.7$  mmol/L ( $< 150$  mg/dL) indicates lower risk and higher levels indicate a need to look for other risk factors" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/su_verified_0074e29f31a1f0feb082e0064bee46f60bf6b5ae3f8703d1231341374ed97e52_table_1/e_0083> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://digistrucmed.org/ExtractedEntity> .
