<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/During%20the%20initial%20phases%20%28duration%20based%20on%20individual%20features%29%20supervised%2C%20in-hospital%20exercise%20training%20programme%20may%20be%20recommended%2C%20especially%2C%20to%20verify%20individual%20responses%20and%20tolerability%2C%20clinical%20stability%2C%20and%20promptly%20identify%20signs%20and%20symptoms%20indicating%20to%20modify%20or%20terminate%20the%20programme.%20The%20supervision%20should%20include%20physical%20examination%2C%20monitoring%20of%20HR%2C%20BP%20and%20rhythm%20before%2C%20during%20and%20after%20exercise%20training.%20The%20supervised%20period%20should%20be%20prolonged%20in%20patients%20with%20new%20symptoms%2C%20signs%2C%20BP%20abnormalities%20and%20increased%20supraventricular%20or%20ventricular%20ectopy%20during%20exercise> <http://digistrucmed.org/name> "During the initial phases (duration based on individual features) supervised, in-hospital exercise training programme may be recommended, especially, to verify individual responses and tolerability, clinical stability, and promptly identify signs and symptoms indicating to modify or terminate the programme. The supervision should include physical examination, monitoring of HR, BP and rhythm before, during and after exercise training. The supervised period should be prolonged in patients with new symptoms, signs, BP abnormalities and increased supraventricular or ventricular ectopy during exercise" .
